SUMMARY:Inprint Cool Brains! Series presents Elizabeth Acevedo
DTSTAMP:20260816T033420Z
DTSTART:20261018T140000Z
DESCRIPTION: \n\nFree and open to the public\nFree copies of Anger Is Only 
	a Shadow for the first 100 families\nPresentation and Q&A by the author\nM
	eet the author followed by a book sale and signing\nAppearance by celebrat
	ed Houston writer Jasminne Mendez\nBus scholarships available for student 
	groups – full scholarships for public schools\, partial scholarships for p
	rivate schools upon availability. For information\, email info@inprint.org
	\n\nBooks available through Kindred Stories\n\n\nAnd more!\n\n\nThe 2026/2
	027 Inprint Cool Brains! Series proudly presents National Book Award winne
	r and renowned poet Elizabeth Acevedo\, sharing her new YA novel Anger Is 
	Only a Shadow. \nKnown for YA novels filled with poetry\, humor\, and hear
	t\, Elizabeth Acevedo is the New York Times-bestselling author of The Poet
	 X\, which won the National Book Award for Young People’s Literature\, the
	 Michael L. Printz Award\, the Pura Belpré Award\, the Carnegie medal\, th
	e Boston Globe–Horn Book Award\, and the Walter Award. She is also the aut
	hor of With the Fire on High\, which was named a best book of the year by 
	the New York Public Library\, NPR\, Publishers Weekly\, and School Library
	 Journal\; and Clap When You Land\, which was a Boston Globe–Horn Book Hon
	or book and a Kirkus finalist. Acevedo is a National Poetry Slam Champion 
	and served as the 2022 Young People’s Poet Laureate. \n“An irresistible st
	ory of family connection\, resilience\, and loyalty” (Kirkus starred revie
	w)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow is Acevedo’s powerful new YA novel in prose an
	d poetry. Lil is anything but small. She’s rebellious\, she’s loyal\; she’
	s figuring out what kind of good person she wants to be\, or if she wants 
	to be a good person at all. But more than anything? Lil wants to be free. 
	When her instinct for freedom leads to another stay in D.C. juvenile deten
	tion\, Lil knows she’s lucky to just be on probation. But judgment\, guilt
	\, and an ankle monitor weigh heavily on her\, and she can’t shake that pi
	nned-down feeling. The only person who might understand is her big brother
	\, Aldwin. Except he’s more distant now than just the hundred miles from h
	is college. As her court hearing ticks closer\, a question looms over Lil 
	as the missed phone calls and strange texts from her brother pile up: will
	 she stay put\, or put her future freedom on the line? “A striking and nua
	nced portrait of the realities of juvenile detention and mental illness” (
	Publisher’s Weekly starred review) and “intensely genuine” (The Bulletin o
	f the Center for Children’s Books starred review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow
	 is a white-knuckle journal to self-understanding and doing the right thin
	g\, no matter the cost. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-coo
	l-brains-series-presents-elizabeth-acevedo/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-el
	izabeth-acevedo/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
